{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1322,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","line":2253,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Existence of Oriented Orthonormal Frames]\n\\label{prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-orientation, lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames, def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(M,g)$ is a Riemannian $n$-manifold with smooth orientation $o$, every $p\\in M$ has a neighbourhood with a smooth local frame that is orthonormal and positively oriented at every point.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-orientation,lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation,prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\\sketch Start with a smooth positively oriented frame supplied by Definition \\ref{def:smooth-orientation}. Fibrewise Gram--Schmidt gives a smooth orthonormal frame by Proposition \\ref{prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}, and Lemma \\ref{lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation} preserves its orientation.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Existence of Oriented Orthonormal Frames] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a6f7269656e7465642d6f7274686f6e6f726d616c2d6672616d6573\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\">↗ def:smooth-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Agram-schmidt-preserves-orientation\">↗ lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:existence-orthonormal-frames</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is a Riemannian <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold with smooth orientation <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o$\">$o$</span>, every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> has a neighbourhood with a smooth local frame that is orthonormal and positively oriented at every point.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\">↗ def:smooth-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Agram-schmidt-preserves-orientation\">↗ lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:existence-orthonormal-frames</a> \\sketch Start with a smooth positively oriented frame supplied by Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a736d6f6f74682d6f7269656e746174696f6e\">12</a>. Fibrewise Gram–Schmidt gives a smooth orthonormal frame by Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a6578697374656e63652d6f7274686f6e6f726d616c2d6672616d6573\">4</a>, and Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Agram-schmidt-preserves-orientation\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6772616d2d7363686d6964742d7072657365727665732d6f7269656e746174696f6e\">12</a> preserves its orientation. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","label":"def:smooth-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation","title":"lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation","label":"lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","label":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-determinant","title":"prop:volume-form-determinant","label":"prop:volume-form-determinant"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","label":"prop:volume-form-value-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-coframe","title":"prop:volume-form-coframe","label":"prop:volume-form-coframe"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-smooth","title":"prop:volume-form-smooth","label":"prop:volume-form-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","title":"lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","label":"lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Existence of Oriented Orthonormal Frames]\n\\label{prop:oriented-orthonormal-frames}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-orientation, lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames, def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(M,g)$ is a Riemannian $n$-manifold with smooth orientation $o$, every $p\\in M$ has a neighbourhood with a smooth local frame that is orthonormal and positively oriented at every point.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-orientation,lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation,prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\\sketch Start with a smooth positively oriented frame supplied by Definition \\ref{def:smooth-orientation}. Fibrewise Gram--Schmidt gives a smooth orthonormal frame by Proposition \\ref{prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}, and Lemma \\ref{lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation} preserves its orientation.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation","title":"lem:gram-schmidt-preserves-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}